            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="SHE05" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John Baker</forename>
                        <surname>Holroyd</surname>
                        <addName>earl of Sheffield</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1741-12-21">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1821-05-30"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Holroyd, John Baker, first earl of Sheffield (1741–1821), politician. 
   See entry of 8 May 1788: 'Dinner at Cadel's on Gibbon's birth day and day of publication, Sheffield, Fullaston, 
  Reynolds, Gillies, Kippis.'</p>
                        <p>The identification of this entry seems certain, given Holroyd's close friendship with Gibbon and his editorship of Gibbon's work after his death.</p>
                        <p>There is then a long absence, but with one Miss Sheff'd, not recorded here, Sheffield reappears on 30 August 1806 in company with Boaden, 
    and then in 1808, with Planta and K Courtenay.
  There is more uncertainty about the second and third entries, but both are possible.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
